From a2ff3dfbf5d2d031da911d492d1972760429a486 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:50:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] Round 4: Serialize typed metrics instead of a JSON
 value map

The domain returns a typed Metrics struct whose fields are declared in
the alphabetical key order of the former serde_json::Value map, so
records keep their exact bytes while skipping per-record key strings,
map inserts and boxed numbers. Failure metrics keep the Value form
behind an untagged enum. The trace remains a Value in this round. A
unit test checks the metrics key order for traced and untraced rows.

Workload: serial (96 full records, 62 steps each, one worker).
Before median: 0.1834 ms. After median: 0.1062 ms. Speedup: 1.73x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
